CAT = "s6Profile"; SEG = "PRO"
Q = [
('For a non-U.S. person opening an account, a customer identification program may accept, in place of a taxpayer ID:',
 'Passport number and country', ['A utility bill', 'A letter from a bank officer', 'An email address'],
 'Under the CIP rule, a non-U.S. person may give a taxpayer ID, a passport number and issuing country, an alien ID card number, or another government ID number.'),
('Under Regulation S-P, after the initial notice a firm generally gives customers a privacy notice:',
 'Once a year', ['At each trade', 'Every five years', 'Only on request'],
 'Regulation S-P requires an annual privacy notice during the customer relationship, with a narrow exception when the firm\'s policies have not changed and it shares only within set limits.'),
('A full power of attorney, unlike a limited one, lets the agent:',
 'Trade and withdraw assets', ['Only enter trades', 'Only view account statements', 'Only update mailing addresses'],
 'A limited power of attorney allows trading only. A full power of attorney also lets the agent withdraw cash and securities from the account.'),
('A power of attorney over a customer\'s brokerage account ends when the customer:',
 'Dies', ['Turns 75', 'Moves to another state', 'Changes reps'],
 'Every power of attorney ends at the principal\'s death; the account then passes under the estate\'s control. A durable power survives incapacity, not death.'),
('Under Rule 3260, each discretionary order a rep enters must be:',
 'Promptly approved in writing', ['Reported to FINRA each month', 'Confirmed by phone first', 'Limited to five a month'],
 'Rule 3260 requires the firm, through a designated person, to approve each discretionary order promptly in writing and to review the account for excessive trading.'),
('Rule 2090 requires a firm to use reasonable diligence to know each customer\'s essential facts:',
 'At opening and while open', ['Only before margin use', 'Only for large accounts', 'Only after a complaint'],
 'Know your customer applies to the opening and maintenance of every account, so the facts must be kept current while the relationship lasts.'),
('Reasonable-basis suitability is met when a rep\'s diligence shows a product is:',
 'Fit for at least some investors', ['Certain to rise in value over time', 'Right for every customer', 'Free of all sales charges'],
 'Rule 2111 requires the rep to understand a product well enough to believe it suits at least some investors before recommending it to anyone.'),
('A rep recommends a fund that suits many investors but not this customer\'s needs. Which obligation is missed?',
 'Customer-specific', ['Reasonable-basis', 'Quantitative', 'Best-execution obligation'],
 'Customer-specific suitability asks whether the recommendation fits this customer\'s investment profile. A product can pass reasonable-basis review and still fail for one customer.'),
('Under Rule 2111, an explicit recommendation to hold a fund is:',
 'Covered by suitability', ['Never a recommendation', 'Exempt from the profile', 'Covered only for stocks'],
 'Supplementary material to Rule 2111 treats an explicit recommendation to hold a security as a recommended strategy that must be suitable.'),
('Reg BI\'s disclosure obligation requires telling a retail customer, at or before a recommendation:',
 'Material facts and conflicts', ['The rep\'s home address', 'Other clients\' trades', 'The firm\'s yearly profits and losses'],
 'Reg BI requires full and fair disclosure of the material facts of the relationship, including fees and services, and of conflicts tied to the recommendation.'),
('Reg BI requires broker-dealers to eliminate which practice?',
 'Short-term product sales contests', ['Commissions on fund sales', 'Any pay that varies with sales volume', 'Fee-based advisory accounts'],
 'Reg BI\'s conflict obligation requires firms to identify and eliminate sales contests, quotas, bonuses and non-cash compensation based on selling specific securities within a limited period.'),
('A paper Form CRS for a firm that is only a broker-dealer is limited to:',
 'Two pages', ['One page', 'Four pages', 'Ten pages'],
 'Form CRS instructions limit a stand-alone broker-dealer or adviser to two pages on paper, and a dual registrant to four.'),
('Under Rule 2214, an investment analysis tool used with customers must come with disclosure of:',
 'Its assumptions and limits', ['The rep\'s personal past returns', 'A guaranteed outcome', 'A forecast of next year\'s index'],
 'Rule 2214 allows probability tools if the firm describes the criteria and methodology, explains the assumptions and limitations, and states that results are hypothetical.'),
('Under a firm\'s Rule 3110 procedures, new accounts are reviewed and approved by:',
 'A registered principal', ['Any registered rep', 'The customer\'s accountant', 'The clearing firm\'s CEO'],
 'Rule 3110 requires supervisory procedures, and account opening approval is done by a principal or designated supervisor, who signs to show acceptance.'),
('A firm should not open an account when the customer:',
 'Will not give required ID data', ['Has never owned securities before', 'Lives in another state', 'Wants only mutual funds'],
 'If a customer refuses the identifying information the CIP requires or cannot be verified, the firm\'s program must say when it will not open the account.'),
('A customer hands a rep a check payable to the rep personally to buy fund shares. The rep should:',
 'Have it reissued to the firm', ['Deposit it, then pay the fund', 'Endorse it to the fund company', 'Cash it and send a firm check'],
 'Customer payments for securities must be made to the broker-dealer or the fund, never to the rep. Taking a personal check invites conversion and must be avoided.'),
]
